  "finding": {
    "id": "B2-LC-01",
    "classification": "Reproducible B2 recovery-event contract gap / recovery-end misattribution; not an R1 projectile emission, scheduler completion, or gameplay cooldown defect.",
    "scope": "B2 event metadata for natural sweep recovery; no R2/R3 classification change.",
    "reproducedIn": [
      "pogo",
      "matarife",
      "traidor",
      "nucleo"
    ],
    "observedCounts": {
      "naturalSweepStarts": 4,
      "attackEnds": 4,
      "matchingRecoveryStartEvents": 0,
      "recoveryEndTaggedSweepBeforeSweepEnd": 4,
      "actualTailRecoveryEnds": 4
    },
    "mechanism": "During each natural sweep, the preceding pattern recovery timer remains live while syncCombatSignals changes rec.pattern to sweep. advance() later emits recovery.end using rec.pattern, so the prior recovery end is tagged sweep. When the sweep reaches its fire tail, the normal sweep branch emits attack.end and sets rec.recovery but does not emit recovery.start; the later sweep-removal branch only emits recovery.start if rec.attackActive is still true, which is already false after the normal fire-window end. The FSM still enters ATTACK_RECOVERY and emits recovery.end for the 0.3-second sweep tail.",
    "sourceLocations": "boss_animation_state_machine.js:257-271 (sweep pattern/recovery and attack.end; no recovery.start); 273-279 (recovery.start only if attackActive on sweep removal); 343-345 (recovery.end uses current rec.pattern).",
    "impact": "Pattern attacks retain one start/end/recovery.start per normal completed run. Sweep attacks each have one start/end, one subsequent ATTACK_RECOVERY state and a tail recovery.end; however B2 emits no recovery.start for the sweep tail and emits one preceding recovery.end tagged as sweep. No duplicate attack starts/terminals, projectile counter mismatch, or attack overlap was found.",
    "action": "No code changes under B4.2. Documented for owner triage; stop advancement pending authorization."
  },
